1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,372
Bombs Aimed at Oil

2
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:29,768
Before dawn on March 8 the Israeli Air Force bombed Iran’s oil facilities for the first time in the war. Four people were killed. Black smoke from the storage tanks spread over the capital. The sun came up and it did not get light. There were fears of fuel shortages, of poisoned water and soil, of damage to people’s lungs. The war’s targets were moving from military sites to the country’s livelihood.

3
00:00:30,368 --> 00:00:55,300
The same day U.S. and Israeli forces said they had hit the Revolutionary Guards’ Aerospace Force headquarters and 50 ammunition depots. CENTCOM announced a seventh American service member killed by Iranian attacks. In Kuwait City a drone set a high-rise on fire, and two Kuwaiti officers died on duty. A third U.S. aircraft carrier was on its way to the Middle East.

4
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:22,464
On March 9 the Assembly of Experts named Mojtaba Khamenei, the dead leader’s second son, as the new Supreme Leader. He had never held public office. The same day the Safavid palaces of Chehel Sotoun and Ali Qapu in Isfahan were badly damaged. An explosion near Manama, Bahrain, injured 32 people, and the state oil company BAPCO declared force majeure.

5
00:01:23,064 --> 00:01:26,804
Epic Fury continues in Episode 5.
